sizeof a dereferenced array does not step the type twice.

MEASURED, and only one of three spellings was wrong:

    static char* pa[3];
    sizeof(pa)      24        right
    sizeof(pa[0])    8        right
    sizeof(*pa)      1        WRONG -- should be 8

A declaration `T name[N]` records T in the symbol's type and N in
array_modifier, so the type held there is the ELEMENT before any star is
applied. Stepping once more gave what the element points AT -- char, for an
array of char*.

AN ARRAY OF long HID IT. `sizeof(*arr)` on `long arr[3]` came out 8 and
correct, because long's own ->type is long: the extra step lands back where it
started. Only an array whose element is a POINTER shows it, and case 108 --
written for exactly this family after tccelf.c's sym_attr table -- uses a
pointer VARIABLE rather than an array of them.

WHAT IT COST. tcc chooses its library-search format like this:

    static const char * const libs[] = { "%s/lib%s.so", "%s/lib%s.a", NULL };
    ...
    if (s->static_link)
        pp += sizeof(libs) / sizeof(*libs) - 2;             libtcc.c:1130

24/1 - 2 is 22, so `pp` landed far past the array and `*pp` was a pointer into
unrelated data. Probed from inside mc-tcc, every -l search built a path one
character long:

    LIB fmt=P path=/usr/lib name=c   ->  [P]
    LIB fmt=P path=/lib     name=c   ->  [P]

so mc-tcc segfaulted on any link that resolved a library BY NAME. Explicit
paths worked, which is why it survived every -nostdlib test: those pass their
objects outright. Only a HOSTED link takes that branch -- rung 3 of the
stage-4 ladder, the first rung that needs `-lc`, and the same crash
tcc-two-ways has reported for weeks at "does it compile anything at all".

GREATER THAN ONE, NOT NON-ZERO, and this is the part worth keeping. The first
version of the fix tested `t->array_modifier != 0`. array_modifier DEFAULTS to
1 for every symbol (cc_core.c:186) and only an actual array sets it higher --
which is why the sites at 1765 and 1940 test `> 1` and `<= 1`. The `!= 0`
version fired for plain pointers too and made `sizeof(*p)` 8 instead of 16.
Case 108 caught it in the same minute.

MEASURED, LOCALLY, EITHER SIDE:

    difftest amd64       99 -> 100 pass, 0 fail   (case 121 new)
    difftest aarch64    101 -> 102 pass, 0 fail
    stage 2 corpus      419 of 426                unchanged
    tests2 via mc-tcc    90 of 105                unchanged
    self-compilation     gen2.o == gen3.o         unchanged

    a HOSTED static link -- crt1.o, libc.a and -lc resolved by name --
    now produces an executable BYTE-IDENTICAL to the gcc-built control's,
    1896 bytes, and it runs.

